    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d266">

                <pb facs="0441" n="347" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg347"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lincoln to Mr.
                            Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-02-01"><hi rendition="#italic">February 1,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 906.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instructions numbered
                    969, of November 21, and to Mr. White’s dispatch No. 860, of December 6, 1892, I
                    have the honor to inclose herewith a copy of a note which I have received from
                    Lord Rosebery in reply to that which Mr. White addressed to his lordship on the
                    5th of December last, relative to the restrictions upon the importation of
                    cattle from the United States to Great Britain, and of which a copy was
                    transmitted to you in his dispatch aforesaid.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert T.
                    Lincoln.</hi></signed></closer>




